-- title:
--   Coset conjugates as roots of Φ_N(j(q^N),Y)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let `data` be a modular-polynomial packet of level $N$: a polynomial $\Phi =$ `data.Φ` in $\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ which is monic, whose degree equals `dedekindPsi N` $=\sum_{d\mid N,\ d\text{ squarefree}} N/d$, and which satisfies $\Phi(\mathrm{jq}, \mathrm{jqN}\,N) = 0$ in the Laurent series field over $\mathbb Q$, the coefficients of $\Phi$ being evaluated at the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant. The assertion is that there exists a unit $\zeta$ of $\mathbb C$ which is a primitive $N$-th root of unity such that the following holds for every triple $t=(a,b,d)$ in `primCosetReps N`, that is, every triple of naturals at most $N$ with $ad=N$, $b<d$ and $\gcd(a,\gcd(b,d))=1$: the Laurent series `cosetConj ζ (jqModC ℂ) t` is a root of the one-variable polynomial over $\mathbb C((q))$ obtained from $\Phi$ by mapping each coefficient in $\mathbb Z[X]$ through the ring homomorphism sending $X$ to `qExpand ℂ N (jqModC ℂ)`. Here `jqModC ℂ` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ over $\mathbb C$, i.e. the integral expansion $j(q)=q^{-1}+744+\cdots$; `qExpand ℂ N` is the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb C((q))$ rescaling exponents by $N$, so the first argument is $j(q^N)$; and `cosetConj ζ J (a, b, d)` is $0$ when $a=0$ and otherwise the image of $J$ under `qTwist (ζ ^ (a * b))` followed by `qExpand ℂ (a * a)`, that is $j(\zeta^{ab}q^{a^2})$, the expansion of $j((a\tau+b)/d)$ in the variable $q^{1/N}$. The degenerate case $a=0$ does not occur for triples in `primCosetReps N`.
--
--   This is the formal-series form of the classical statement that each of the $\psi(N)$ functions $j\circ S_{a,b,d}$, with $ad=N$, $0\le b<d$ and $\gcd(a,b,d)=1$, is a root of $\Phi_N(j,Y)$ (Silverman, Advanced Topics, Thm II.6.3(a)). It supplies the list of conjugates used in the analysis of the field generated by the level-$N$ $q$-expansion of $j$ and in the study of automorphisms of modular curves of level $N$ and $\Gamma_0$-type.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ModularPolynomialData_exists_isPrimitiveRoot_forall_isRoot_cosetConj_complex.lean

